    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0169" n="53" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg53"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 893.00/700.</note>
                <head ana="#head_untitled-inferred-from-preceding-sibling-head">[Untitled]</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegrams.—Extracts.—Paraphrases.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Peking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1911-11-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 27, 1911</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>I report with reserve that the Legation has been requested by the Chinese
                    Government to inform the Department that the Japanese <pb facs="0170" n="54"
                        xml:id="pg54"/> are supplying revolutionists in South Manchuria railway zone
                    with funds for arms and recruits and are giving them free passage on trains.
                    Four Japanese are advisers to revolutionists. Japanese also reported arming
                    Hunghutzus. The Viceroy addressed the Japanese Consul General out obtained no
                    satisfaction.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Calhoun.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
